      <h1>How much does a factory website cost in India?</h1>
      <p class="article-meta">By Sutrayaan · Updated {{ page.updated_label }} · 6-minute read</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="prose">
        <p class="answer"><b>Short answer:</b> a website that actually brings enquiries to a small or mid-sized Indian manufacturer costs <b>₹30,000 to ₹75,000</b> to build, plus roughly <b>₹4,000 to ₹16,000 a year</b> to run (domain, hosting and one business email, before any maintenance plan). Template sites cost less, from about ₹5,000, but rarely show what B2B buyers check. Fully custom agency builds start around ₹45,000 and can go well past ₹1 lakh.</p>

        <h2>What the options cost</h2>
        <p>Prices below are typical 2026 market ranges for a 6 to 10 page business website, before GST.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
          <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Typical cost</th><th>Good for</th><th>Watch out for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><b>Do-it-yourself builder</b></td><td>₹0–10,000 + a monthly plan</td><td>A basic online presence, fast</td><td>Your time; generic templates; few B2B features</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>IndiaMART catalogue site</b></td><td>Comes with paid plans, e.g. about ₹28,000–40,000 a year (Mini Dynamic Catalogue) to ₹60,000 a year (Maximiser)<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></td><td>Getting IndiaMART leads</td><td>Template look; buyers see IndiaMART branding and buttons; check what happens to the site if you stop the plan</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Freelancer or template site</b></td><td>₹5,000–25,000<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></td><td>A simple brochure</td><td>Often slow on phones; content left to you; support can disappear</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Small agency brochure or WordPress site</b></td><td>₹20,000–45,000<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></td><td>General small businesses</td><td>They may not know what a machine list, COA or ply rating is</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Manufacturing specialist</b> (like Sutrayaan)</td><td>₹30,000–75,000</td><td>Factories that want B2B enquiries</td><td>Make sure the quote includes content writing and a plant visit</td></tr>
            <tr><td><b>Custom-built agency site</b></td><td>₹45,000–90,000+, larger projects ₹1–3 lakh+<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></td><td>Large catalogues, integrations, portals</td><td>Longer timelines; more than most SMEs need</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <h2>What it costs to keep running each year</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
          <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical yearly cost</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Domain name (.com)</td><td>About ₹1,000</td><td>First-year offers are often cheaper; renewal is around ₹999 at GoDaddy India<sup><a href="#s3">3</a></sup></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>₹0–12,000</td><td>Simple fast sites can cost almost nothing to host; WordPress hosting is usually ₹3,000–12,000<sup><a href="#s2">2</a></sup></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Business email</td><td>About ₹3,200 per person</td><td>Google Workspace's entry plan is about ₹270 per user per month on a yearly plan, before GST<sup><a href="#s4">4</a></sup></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Google Business Profile</td><td>Free</td><td>The single most useful free listing for local buyers</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Updates and maintenance</td><td>₹0–36,000</td><td>Ad hoc changes, or a monthly plan (ours is ₹3,000 a month)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <h2>What pushes the price up</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Number of products.</b> A catalogue of 200 chemicals or 80 machined parts takes longer than 10 product families.</li>
          <li><b>Photography.</b> A proper plant shoot adds cost, but it's the biggest single improvement most factory sites can make.</li>
          <li><b>Languages.</b> Each extra language (Hindi, Marathi) adds writing and checking.</li>
          <li><b>Integrations.</b> Connecting to a CRM, ERP or WhatsApp Business API.</li>
          <li><b>Online selling.</b> Payments, carts and stock are a different, bigger project.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Six questions to ask before you pay</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><b>Who owns the domain?</b> It should be registered in your company's name, not the developer's.</li>
          <li><b>What does it cost after year one?</b> Ask for hosting, domain and support costs in writing.</li>
          <li><b>Who writes the content?</b> If it's you, the site will take months. Good vendors write it after a plant visit.</li>
          <li><b>Can buyers send a drawing or spec?</b> A quote form with file upload beats an email address.</li>
          <li><b>Where do enquiries go?</b> They should reach you instantly and be tracked, not sit in an inbox.</li>
          <li><b>How fast is it on a phone?</b> Ask to see a past site on your own phone, on mobile data.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Is a ₹10,000 website enough?</h2>
        <p>For a shop or a local service, often yes. For a manufacturer selling to purchase managers and engineers, usually not: cheap templates rarely show machines, materials, certifications or a proper RFQ form, and that is exactly what B2B buyers check before they call. The better question is how many lost enquiries a weak site costs you each year.</p>

        <h2>What we charge</h2>
        <p>Sutrayaan websites start at ₹30,000 and most factory sites land between ₹30,000 and ₹75,000, depending on pages and products. That includes writing, a plant visit, a quote form with drawing upload, and Google Business Profile setup, ready in 2–3 weeks. The enquiry tracker is free with a website at launch. Full details are on our <a href="/services/">services page</a>, and you can see what we build on four <a href="/work/">live demo sites</a>.</p>

        <div class="faq" style="margin-top:12px">
          <details><summary>Is it better to pay once or yearly?</summary><p>Pay once for the build, and separately for running costs. Avoid deals where stopping a yearly fee means losing your site or domain.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I keep IndiaMART and have my own website?</summary><p>Yes, and most manufacturers should. Use IndiaMART for marketplace leads and your own site for buyers who search for you directly or check you before placing an order. More in our <a href="/guides/indiamart-vs-own-website/">IndiaMART vs own website guide</a>.</p></details>
          <details><summary>How long does a factory website take?</summary><p>Two to three weeks for most sites, if photos and product details are ready. Large catalogues take longer.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Do I need to hire a photographer?</summary><p>Not always. One planned visit with a good phone camera and daylight covers most needs; a professional shoot is worth it for export-focused sites.</p></details>
        </div>

